3. Data
-------

Ink presets (src/inks.js)
  - Generic stock shades, the sim-process kit and the skin add-ons:
    ADN's own approximate sRGB values. No third-party data.
  - Wilflex Epic Rio: product names and codes as Avient lists them
    (facts); the colors are ADN's own visual estimates, because Wilflex
    publishes no color values.
  - FN-INK: product names only (facts, used to name the products).
    The colors are ADN's own estimates: each product is ADN's generic
    shade of the same color name, or an equal mix of two of them in the
    print model's mixing space (src/inks.js, estimateFromGeneric). No
    FN-INK published color values are used. They are replaced by
    press-run readings when a shop imports its measured drawdowns.
  Product names are trademarks of their owners. ADN is not affiliated
  with Avient, Wilflex or FN-INK. The tool ships no PANTONE data.

ICC profiles
  None bundled. icc.js reads the profile embedded in the user's own
  image and converts to the sRGB profile Little CMS builds in memory
  (cmsCreate_sRGBProfile).

Test images
  test-images/04 to 18 are made by scripts/make-test-images.py (ADN,
  no third-party content). test-images/01 to 03 are ADN synthetic test
  images (flat shapes, gradients and lettering; no third-party
  content); no script in this tree draws them. benchmark/truth/*.png
  are made by benchmark/truth/make.py. All of these are covered by the
  MIT License.
  test-images/19 to 30 are photographs of works in the public domain,
  from the Art Institute of Chicago, released by the museum under
  Creative Commons Zero (CC0). test-images/SOURCES.md lists each
  work, its museum record and the file's SHA-256.

src/assets/brand/
  The Separation Table marks, made by ADN. The PNGs and favicon.ico
  are rendered from the SVGs by scripts/render-icons.mjs;
  social-1200x630.png is a layout made by ADN.

src/assets/adn-mark-still.svg
  The ADN logo. It is a trademark of American Dream Network, LLC and is
  not covered by the MIT License grant.

Fonts: none bundled.


4. Published methods implemented here
-------------------------------------

These are implemented in ADN's own code from the cited publications. The
code comments cite them; no third-party source code is ported.

  CIEDE2000 color difference: Sharma, Wu and Dalal, "The CIEDE2000
    color-difference formula", Color Research and Application, 2005
    (src/engine.js)
  Delta E CMC(l:c): CMC of the Society of Dyers and Colourists
    (checked against color.js)
  Yule-Nielsen modified spectral Neugebauer / mixing in linear
    reflectance (src/engine.js, src/calib.js)
  Demichel equations for rotated-screen overprint (README "How it
    separates")
  Palette from the convex hull of the art's colors, after Tan,
    Echevarria and Gingold, "Efficient palette-based decomposition and
    recoloring of images via RGBXY-space geometry", 2018 (src/engine.js)
  FISTA (fast iterative shrinkage-thresholding) least squares
    (src/engine.js)
  Euclidean projection onto the simplex, sort-based, Duchi et al. 2008
    (src/engine.js)
  OKLab, Bjorn Ottosson, 2020 (src/engine.js)
  Floyd-Steinberg error diffusion, vector form in mix space (index mode)
  Ordered 8x8 Bayer threshold (src/engine.js)
  Standard halftone screen angles per print method: The Print Guide,
    "Halftone screen angles", 2009 (src/plan.js)

Published values (src/plan.js FABRICS and builtinProfiles, cited in
src/help.js).
Values are restated in our words; no text is copied beyond short facts.
  Garment fabrics: Avient, Wilflex Epic Polywhite LC technical data
    sheet V3.04 (2023); Wilflex Ink Curing Tips (2020); Wilflex Product
    Selection Guide (2024); Rutland Ink Guide (Avient); International
    Coatings 741 Ultra LB White technical data sheet (2011); Impressions
    magazine, "Fewer Problems with Poly" (Laster, 2020) and "Screen
    Printing on Fleece" (Ortolani, 2014); ScreenPrinting.com, "The 4
    most common types of t-shirts" (Wedman, 2023); The Shirt Board,
    fleece choke (Colin, 2014). No source gives dot gain by fabric.
  Built-in press profiles: UltraSeps film output settings (Roginski,
    2015); The Shirt Board (blue moon, 2013 and 2018); ScreenPrinting.com
    help, halftone mesh; T-Biz Network (Fresener, 2018); Impressions
    magazine (Ortolani, 2014). Values without a source are labelled as
    Separation Table defaults (estimates). None is press-tested.

